# Study-specific working dirs (NEVER commit client data)
#
# inputs/ is DEFAULT-DENY and WORKSPACE-ONLY. Anything dropped here is
# presumed to be real study material and must never reach a commit --
# `git add -A` cannot sweep it in. The training example ships inside the
# package (arsbridge_example()), not here. Only two files are tracked: this
# folder's README, and the public pharmaverseadam-derived ADaM spec, which
# data-raw/build_example_bundle.R regenerates. The allowlist names it
# EXACTLY -- no wildcard, so no pattern can ever brush against a sponsor
# file's name.
inputs/*
!inputs/README.md
!inputs/adam_spec_CDSC-ALZ-201.xlsx
# inputs/DRM/ holds the retired APX-DRM-301 dermatology example, kept on
# this machine only.
inputs/DRM/

# Local planning / handoff notes. These describe work against real studies
# and are written for one machine, not for the repo. Kept out of commits by
# default; `git add -f` if one is ever genuinely worth publishing.
HANDOFF_*.md

# Redacted transfer artifacts from a restricted machine (tools/README_privacy_transfer.md).
# Structure-only by construction, but they describe a real study and belong to
# the debugging session, not to the package.
digest.json
ars_digest.json
diagnostics_redacted.csv
*_digest.json
*_redacted.csv

RWE_error/
# suprev/ holds local Copilot working files (blueprints, instruction
# drafts, conformance notes) tied to a specific study -- never committed.
suprev/
inputs/ADaM/
outputs/
.align_backup/
inputs/.shell_backup/
graphify-out/
~$*
scratch_*.R
run_*.R
.siera_ref/
